60,3,1,talk,Minato,,Plan A uses gravel and trees. The firms can handle that. Plan B needs deep foundations for the stalls.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, Plan A is the only one the habitat fund fully covers. Plan B is a money pit.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Plan A matches the volunteers' skills. They can tend the trees. The old basin shows water works if we let it.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@May, Plan A needs less daily staff. The casual pool can manage the gravel paths. Plan C is too complex.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Plan A provides shade and a clear route. The drainage works with the trees. It matches the people's flow.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,I am worried about Plan D. The reshaping is too risky for the clay. Plan A is safer for the ground.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, Plan A minimizes hard surfaces. The upkeep cost is the lowest. It is the only financially sound choice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Plan A respects the past. The green spaces have survived. The paved areas have not. Let us choose the green.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,I am concerned about Plan C. The courts need constant maintenance. We do not have the staff. Plan A is manageable.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,Plan D fights the heat. Plan B ignores the foot traffic. Plan A works with the site. It is the rational choice.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, Plan A is realistic. The local firms can finish it on time. I feel confident in this choice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, the numbers back you up. Plan A is affordable now and in three years. It is the only option that survives.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I am smiling. The volunteers are ready. The land is ready. Plan A is the gentle, enduring choice.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I am relieved. Plan A matches our capacity. The casual pool can handle it. It is the only plan that will last.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The data is unanimous. The site wants shade, drainage, and a clear path. Plan A delivers exactly that.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I am ready to vote. Plan A is safe for the ground and the budget. I trust the local firms with it.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,I am ready to vote. Plan A is the only plan that does not bankrupt the city. It is the responsible choice.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am ready to vote. Plan A honors the past and the people. It is the kind, lasting choice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I am ready to vote. Plan A matches the staff and the volunteers. It is the only plan that will be maintained.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I am ready to vote. Plan A works with the water and the walkers. It is the only plan that makes sense.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
